{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/63455-solar-steath-no-more-sushi-i-mean-umi","id":63455,"title":"Solar Steath: No more Sushi....I mean UMI !","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-02T08:49:51-08:00","id":63455,"title":"Solar Steath: No more Sushi....I mean UMI !","content":"I know that some crazy people think that Solar should not do subtle stuff 'cause they are the chosen of the ~SUN~ or something, but since I really really really hate the Jedi Mind-trick charm in the Core book so.....more real ninja charm in Ex3 instead of weird Malfeas-esque <i>Sneaking By Shouting I'M-NOT-HERE Method</i>, please ~ ? <br /> <br /> P/s: And Solardesperately in need of high-Essence Stealth charms so the crazy people above won't go nuclear and citing &quot;Eyes of Conky &gt; Invisible Statue Spirit, therefore there are a constant cosmic rule in Creation that make Awareness &gt; Stealth which mean that Truth &gt; Lie&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T09:53:05-08:00","id":63472,"title":"","content":"Someone on the old forums (Lioness, I think?) said that the UMI of Solar Stealth works the way it does because it's less of an &quot;IGNORE ME!&quot; effect and more of an &quot;Avert your gaze from the sun&quot; type deal. 'cause really, when was the last time you looked directly at the sun and were able to see it?<br /> <br /> It's very similar to how the Jedi use the Force for stealth. They subtly alter the minds of others so that they're tagged as &quot;ignorable&quot; or &quot;unimportant&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T10:06:37-08:00","id":63481,"title":"","content":"The specific execution with the UMI was clumsy but the thematic intent was sound.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T10:24:25-08:00","id":63489,"title":"","content":"Well, I do know that it is a thesis statement that high-end awareness trumps high-end stealth...<br /> <br /> But yeah, something a bit less overtly jedi mind trick would probably be a good idea. I mean, I can see why they made it that way, but more impossible feats and less bamboozling of the enemy would be a good alternative track, I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/673-requiem_jeer","name":"Requiem_Jeer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar673_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T10:32:47-08:00","id":63493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/63455-solar-steath-no-more-sushi-i-mean-umi?p=63472#post63472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Someone on the old forums (Lioness, I think?) said that the UMI of Solar Stealth works the way it does because it's less of an &quot;IGNORE ME!&quot; effect and more of an &quot;<b>Avert your gaze from the sun</b>&quot; type deal. 'cause really, when was the last time you looked directly at the sun and were able to see it?<br /> <br /> It's very similar to how the Jedi use the Force for stealth. They subtly alter the minds of others so that they're tagged as &quot;ignorable&quot; or &quot;unimportant&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Too much Sidereal-ness in my Solar charmset is bad m'kay. Why it's so hard to give Solar invisible charm instead of all the &quot;I'm really should be in Performance&quot; charms in the Core book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T10:36:50-08:00","id":63495,"title":"","content":"The main character from <i>3-Iron</i> is my go-to example for how Solar Stealth should look.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1564-shinjo","name":"Shinjo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T10:48:22-08:00","id":63497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/63455-solar-steath-no-more-sushi-i-mean-umi?p=63493#post63493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Too much Sidereal-ness in my Solar charmset is bad m'kay. Why it's so hard to give Solar invisible charm instead of all the &quot;I'm really should be in Performance&quot; charms in the Core book.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not certain how &quot;avert your gaze from the sun&quot; translates to &quot;Sidereal&quot;. Solars are allowed esoteric effects like any other Exalt since one of their major themes is Sunlight, although it's less prominent since their other major themes are &quot;perfection&quot; and &quot;superhuman skill&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T11:18:08-08:00","id":63509,"title":"","content":"In 2e, Solar Stealth covers a very broad range of effects; compelling people not to notice them is one approach, but not their only approach.<br /> <br /> Easily-Overlooked Presence simply makes you hard to spot; nothing in it suggests it works via mental influence, and mental defenses don't help you against it at all. And Invisible Statue Spirit simply makes you invisible. And their most powerful stealth charm is of course probably IAM, which when used by a dedicated stealth Night caste realistically makes you impossible to detect unless you're going up against someone who expects you.<br /> <br /> As for EotUCS beating Invisible Statue Spirit... I mean, we've been told that 3e will have fewer hard scenelong counter kinds of charms (because they're a bit boring), but the basic idea that active counters to stealth need to be able to beat stealth for them to be worthwhile is sound. Stealth is about your target not knowing you're there. EotUCS can't be kept up permanently, so if they know to activate one of the most expensive charms in the game, you're probably screwed, yes, because the fact that they know to activate EotUCS means you've already failed at stealth.<br /> <br /> Or another way of looking at it: Anti-stealth charms are only useful in one specific situation (when you're going up against stealth.) Stealthiness, though, is useful almost all the time, <i>even against people who have perfect anti-stealth charms</i>, as long as your target isn't actively using the very best and most expensive detective charms right then and there.<br /> <br /> (In fact, as I pointed out above, 2e actually gave far too big of an advantage to stealth even in a Night Stealth Ninja vs. Night Awareness Watchman matchup, because the Ultimate Awareness Guy can't keep IAM up for Awareness all the time -- and the Stealth guy gets to choose when he's going to sneak past, so he will <i>always</i> have IAM for Stealth up when it counts. This means that realistically, the Stealth guy will have a massively larger dice pool and will trivially sneak past an Ultimate Watchman who has lots of excellent charms that he won't get a chance to use.)<br /> <br /> Obviously things are a bit different if you want to use stealth in combat, but at that point you're slipping into a bottomless abyss of 2e problems (starting with the fact that unexpected attacks are instadeath if you don't have a way to totally negate them, which makes everything related to combat stealth completely fall apart).<br /> <br /> But if we're talking about it in the abstract, look at it like a rock-paper-scissors thing. Stealth as a strategy beats obvious strength, which beats alertness, which beats stealth. If you try to focus exclusively on stealth to the exclusion of everything else, you're sometimes going to run into a situation where everyone is on-guard and stealth is, at the very least, severely disadvantaged -- &quot;STEALTH NO LONGER WORKS FOR THE REST OF THE SCENE PERIOD FULLSTOP&quot; might be too extreme, sure, but using stealth tactics is inherently a losing hand against people who can anticipate exactly when, where, and how you're going to approach. That's in the nature of what it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 02-02-2014, 02:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T11:23:44-08:00","id":63512,"title":"","content":"It's funny: the core book goes out of it's way to say this:<br /> <br /> Unnatural mental influence is magical mental influence.<br /> <b>Targets recognize the supernatural force behind the character\u2019s<br /> actions</b>. If this influence is hostile, inappropriate, or used against<br /> targets who value their liberty and independence, unnatural<br /> mental influence makes enemies.<br /> <br /> And then proceeds to treat UMI as the subtlest shit ever. (re: Stealth)<br /> <br /> So, you're a guard, right? And are guarding something. You don't see anyone, but you <i>recognize that some supernatural force is fucking with your mind</i>.<br /> And even if you choose to ignore it (which, unless it's compatible with your Motivation, you can't, so you <i>must</i> spend wp to resist it (Core p.180-181)) as a bad feeling and nothing more, you can still tell your superiors &quot;Yeah, I didn't see anyone but something was fucking with my mind, and then the thing I was guarding was gone&quot;.<br /> <br /> Or you're a shop owner, and a Solar is talking you into lowering your price with UMI. You can actually stop (spend wp to resist) and say &quot;Hey! Stop it with the UMI shit!&quot; or just yell for guards, because UMI is some anathema shit (or so you're told).<br /> <br /> That's kinda... I don't wanna be throwing insults around so I'll say &quot;poorly thought out&quot;. No matter what UMI is used, you will always know there was UMI involved.<br /> &quot;I don't remember what I did (Hypnotic Toungue Tech.), but when that one charismatic-looking dude talked to me I definitely felt his magic getting into my mind and staying.&quot;<br /> <br /> And since characters are actually obligated to spend WP to resist it unless it aligns with their motivation or they want to, everyone you <i>would</i> wanna use it on, would usually be obliged to resist it as much as possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T11:35:09-08:00","id":63516,"title":"","content":"Anyway I think you'll find 3e Stealth satisfying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T11:45:13-08:00","id":63524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/63455-solar-steath-no-more-sushi-i-mean-umi?p=63516#post63516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway I think you'll find 3e Stealth satisfying.</div> </div> </div> </div>There won't be much topic traffic if you and Vance keep using <i>Hope-Spring Eternal Technique </i>on people like that ~","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T12:07:56-08:00","id":63530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/63455-solar-steath-no-more-sushi-i-mean-umi?p=63512#post63512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's funny: the core book goes out of it's way to say this:<br /> <br /> Unnatural mental influence is magical mental influence.<br /> <b>Targets recognize the supernatural force behind the character\u2019s<br /> actions</b>. If this influence is hostile, inappropriate, or used against<br /> targets who value their liberty and independence, unnatural<br /> mental influence makes enemies.<br /> <br /> And then proceeds to treat UMI as the subtlest shit ever. (re: Stealth)<br /> <br /> So, you're a guard, right? And are guarding something. You don't see anyone, but you <i>recognize that some supernatural force is fucking with your mind</i>.<br /> And even if you choose to ignore it (which, unless it's compatible with your Motivation, you can't, so you <i>must</i> spend wp to resist it (Core p.180-181)) as a bad feeling and nothing more, you can still tell your superiors &quot;Yeah, I didn't see anyone but something was fucking with my mind, and then the thing I was guarding was gone&quot;.<br /> <br /> Or you're a shop owner, and a Solar is talking you into lowering your price with UMI. You can actually stop (spend wp to resist) and say &quot;Hey! Stop it with the UMI shit!&quot; or just yell for guards, because UMI is some anathema shit (or so you're told).<br /> <br /> That's kinda... I don't wanna be throwing insults around so I'll say &quot;poorly thought out&quot;. No matter what UMI is used, you will always know there was UMI involved.<br /> &quot;I don't remember what I did (Hypnotic Toungue Tech.), but when that one charismatic-looking dude talked to me I definitely felt his magic getting into my mind and staying.&quot;<br /> <br /> And since characters are actually obligated to spend WP to resist it unless it aligns with their motivation or they want to, everyone you <i>would</i> wanna use it on, would usually be obliged to resist it as much as possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most people's motivations are not going to be contrary to someone sneaking past them. Most people's motivations are probably something like &quot;Live a comfortable life&quot; or &quot;Protect my Family&quot; or something along those lines, and not &quot;Be the best guard ever&quot; or &quot;Protect this castle&quot;. So most NPCs aren't going to *have* to choose to spend the WP, and given that spending WP is supposed to represent a significant exertion (I can't find valid links to Borgstrom's Essay on this, but the system was written under the idea that spending 4 WP was something an NPC would roughly consider equivalent to taking a year off their life. So if the penalty of losing his job or w/e wouldn't ruin his life for at *least* a year, he's not going to spend it...)<br /> <br /> And this is just under the core rules. Once we get to errata, well, you don't notice UMI unless the charm had the Obvious keyword, which the Solar Stealth Charms don't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/782-lafing-cat","name":"Lafing Cat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T12:27:39-08:00","id":63547,"title":"","content":"I run it as the umi can be detected if there is a key. Like an alert or something moving, or a thief getting cocky and stepping on a nightingale floor. Or sets off a trap. At which point the guard would realize something is wrong and be able to shake it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T13:57:09-08:00","id":63589,"title":"","content":"@Laffing Cat (because the &quot;quote&quot; button stopped working): Maybe I'm being pedantic, but the wording seemed to suggest that the action has to specifically align with your motivation for you to not resist, not simply &quot;not go against it&quot;. Bleh, either way I'm happy for the errata (and in my group we've always house-ruled it that way anyway) and am bringing it up more as 2E venting than anything else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T15:58:45-08:00","id":63629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/63455-solar-steath-no-more-sushi-i-mean-umi?p=63512#post63512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's funny: the core book goes out of it's way to say this:<br /> <br /> Unnatural mental influence is magical mental influence. <b>Targets recognize the supernatural force behind the character\u2019s actions</b>. If this influence is hostile, inappropriate, or used against targets who value their liberty and independence, unnaturalmental influence makes enemies.<br /> <br /> And then proceeds to treat UMI as the subtlest shit ever. (re: Stealth)</div> </div> </div> </div>Thankfully, that's been treated with errata:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errata p. 10</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unnatural mental influence does not clearly announce itself as magical mind control unless it comes from an Obvious source and fails to affect the targeted character\u2014characters targeted even by Obvious unnatural mental influence only realize this fact once they have successfully resisted it (although unaffected bystanders who witness an Obvious Charm\u2019s use can tell the target is being subjected to mental coercion of some sort).</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11I0xCPgAS3ZhxGvTlBoePOuaDqgpyWs13jVKhJ4c8hM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Book of the Emerald Circle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/37100-white-elephant-for-flintlock-sidereal-custom-charms-and-discussion-on-themes\" target=\"_blank\">Custom Sidereal Charms</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sQxyi3ox0qn53c_vsUaVQi_pRdpKlQE50NT5ldQmxYI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Expanded Sidereal Linguistics</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/263-limited-reagent","name":"Limited Reagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar263_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}